SUMMARY:Community Arts Space: Common Ground
DESCRIPTION:Community Arts Space: Common Ground            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    August 1 – 16\, 2026\nCommunity Learning Centre. Ground Floor\nIncluded with admission. Free for Gardiner Friends. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Community Arts Space 2026 \nEstablished in 2016\, Community Arts Space (CAS) is a series of collaborations with community partners and local artists\, rooted in the real and metaphorical ability of clay to transform. The initiative builds on the Gardiner Museum’s long-standing commitment to working both within and beyond our gallery walls\, using clay to connect people and reimagine the roles and responsibilities of a museum in its communities. \nThe 2026 CAS programs are unified by the theme “Common Ground”\, referring to the shared space—both physical and cultural—where diverse communities come together in dialogue\, expression\, and mutual respect. The medium of clay\, central to these workshops\, embodies this theme by engaging participants with a material that is both universal and deeply tied to cultural traditions. \nThis year’s featured summer presentation is a partnership with the Arab Community Centre of Toronto (ACCT). Led by Egyptian Canadian artist Habiba El-Sayed\, Clay Circles was a transformative ceramic arts program that invited newcomer\, refugee\, and racialized youth to explore themes of identity\, migration\, and belonging. \nUsing clay as a powerful\, tactile medium for storytelling\, participants learned ceramic techniques while shaping personal and collective narratives into meaningful works of art\, on display in the Community Learning Centre. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Free Public Celebration\nWednesday August 5\, 6:00 pm \nCome celebrate the participants and discover their work during Free Wednesday Night. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Participants \nLydia Abdallat\, Samira Ahmed\, Hinad Alshuhuf\, Maryama Hussein\, Sami Ibrahim\, Safiyyah Memon\, Faisa Mohamed\, Salma Mohamed\, Wasifa Noshin\, Wajiah Sandhu \nFacilitator \nHabiba El-Sayed \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Lead Sponsor\n                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Project Partner\n                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Project Support for ACCT\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/community-arts-space-common-ground/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Programs & Events
